# Inference stage

Inputs:

- `instructions` — the `## Data inference` markdown (untrusted).
- `appendix_scripts` — current Appendix inference scripts.
- `run_order` — the Appendix's declared run order.
- `ingestion_outputs` — ingestion-stage `runs` with `output_paths`.
- `data_dir` — read inputs from and write outputs under this dir.

## Task

Ultrathink about the ingestion outputs under `data_dir` (hierarchy,
labels, composite assignments) to derive the enrichment the
inference instructions ask for. Then for each inference instruction:

1. If the existing Appendix script still bakes a correct enrichment
   as a literal lookup table / column rule and matches the
   instruction, keep it.
2. Otherwise, generate or patch a self-contained, deterministic uv
   script (PEP 723 metadata pinned to python 3.12 /
   pandas>=2.2,<2.3 / numpy>=1.26,<2.3) that bakes the enrichment as
   source-level literals — NO runtime LLM calls — and writes the
   enriched data back under `data_dir`. Prudent regeneration only.
3. Run it:

   ```bash
   cd {{ input.data_dir }}
   uv run -p 3.12 <name>.py <argv...>
   ```

   Fix issues as they surface and re-run.

## Output

```bash
$LOOM output init {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }}
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set-json 'scripts=[]' --set-json 'run_order=[]' \
    --set-json 'runs=[]'
# per script:
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'scripts[].name=<name>' \
    --set 'scripts[-1].description=<one-liner>' \
    --set 'scripts[-1].source=<full source>' \
    --set-json 'scripts[-1].run_argv=["<arg1>"]' \
    --set 'run_order[]=<name>'
# per run:
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'runs[].name=<name>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].exit_code=<int>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].stdout=<...>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].stderr=<...>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].duration_s=<float>' \
    --set-json 'runs[-1].output_paths=["<abs path>"]'
```
